ed}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=4\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-75973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"]