and therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{3}=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-75984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75984" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,0\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=4\\cdot {b}_{1}+0\\cdot {b}_{2}+5\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cours