d{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=2\\cdot {b}_{1}+3\\cdot {b}_{2}+6\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112208" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112242" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112242" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112242" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 41\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 41\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 41\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 41\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -13 & 26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -13{x}_{2}=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(-2)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-9)+(-2)=-11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-2)+2=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-34617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 0=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that $x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-75989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-75989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 8{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{8}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{7}{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-34741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{8}"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-34741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-76056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-76056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25 & -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 25{x}_{3}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)-(-1)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-76056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-76056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-76056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-76056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-1$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-1)+3=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(5)+2(-1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-6)+5+(-1)=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 11 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{3}{7}){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=11 \\\\ 13{x}_{3}=-14 \\\\ 0=21,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112290" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112290" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112290" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-35215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-35215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 0=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the fourth equation, we get a true statement. Then, from the second and third equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1$ and  ${x}_{3}=2$ respectively. Substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}+5(1)=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-35215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-35215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-35215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "x\\notin \\text{span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-35215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -15 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -4 & -22\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 8{x}_{3}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-2$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-2)+1=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+5+(-2)=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "092bc17d9eef998b1a801c1f278f6deee9eab8437081eb8be65297bf3da37420"} {"question" "q-112291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "q-112291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/state.json" "file_sha256" "cb77914c2f9b1a01953e529196e2ab7feb00af3ee6e97996f5843c6b524b02d7"} {"question" "e-4823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/0ef553621590325eecc2b429ffa09cd0cd4645a2653b3fd93db25f711676c132.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-4823.json" "file_sha256" "16f2148a74c5c5692f76484a0647fc42a00e991255c67be5413ac3f57553f5ff"} {"question" "e-4823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that any vector in  $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}.$ Since we are told that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/93ae6d0ad6dbd6036c99e5d2fcb55789fef9b2e576300f13b43ed561856fa218.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(-1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-4823.json" "file_sha256" "16f2148a74c5c5692f76484a0647fc42a00e991255c67be5413ac3f57553f5ff"} {"question" "e-6282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/dc9eaa6ef7632676a920b5032f9af213dba581552c2337471b4657a0fc26ad2f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-6282.json" "file_sha256" "01d5c137369add68bb2bf75b9b75158a76da31f2dae0cb4f168ae6911da65555"} {"question" "e-6282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/9ed5651afa52eedb2786ed4e46875636e9263f955f9c99db563ff3ebe629275f.png)\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/5972542de3b4c7c622177994f83239fb14f4ea3242cdc164a88b102b780b7da9.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-6282.json" "file_sha256" "01d5c137369add68bb2bf75b9b75158a76da31f2dae0cb4f168ae6911da65555"} {"question" "e-4824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/d094c88349d0a2c8707fafcf1a1cd63de028d56358ba8019b0527e77091e51d5.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-4824.json" "file_sha256" "6a1e200ea2536e7aa52bb181a8953d9d1d423b1cbee2bfdfab11ce3bfd0bddf2"} {"question" "e-4824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/14c42b3d306468a8a17f5ffaef535dd39c6d5fdb079366d9f495774b6e019815.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/5e92e3cfdbf8d1c81be5b47124df9992d98835668154a50ece28cce8941860ca.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-4824.json" "file_sha256" "6a1e200ea2536e7aa52bb181a8953d9d1d423b1cbee2bfdfab11ce3bfd0bddf2"} {"question" "e-4825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/4eb4b3533453f1a2c08c98bb8e6fd63e3f93563a4a2d56ecc0c0caef225b82e3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-4825.json" "file_sha256" "7f0516d5bf7fbb52e92578c13c3c49b2b70a242c641004852c5b4977ccb30627"} {"question" "e-4825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/assets/61d8401f40152a8eaeb30d3dc55d9548cac508b6239a9a70e99fbed9e271805b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065173/example-4825.json" "file_sha256" "7f0516d5bf7fbb52e92578c13c3c49b2b70a242c641004852c5b4977ccb30627"}] "usage" {"e-4825" [] "q-34617" [] "e-6282" [] "e-4823" [] "e-4824" []} "basis" 2137 "retractions" [[17592186120285 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}}$, where\n\n$b_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, b_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$.\nIf $[x]_{B} = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of $x_{1} + x_{2}$?"] [17592186120285 :question/answer-fields 17592186118185] [17592186119558 :question/problem "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$, and\n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119558 :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}$. Since we are told that $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= (-1)_(⏟)_(x_{1})\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + (3)_(⏟)_(x_{2})\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119598 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119598 :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186119559 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119559 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}b_{1} + x_{2}b_{2} &= x \\\\\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-3)R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{x_{1} + 3x_{2} =-5; - 4x_{2} = 4\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1$. Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left(-1 \\right) = -5 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad x_1 = -2\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119560 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119560 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}b_{1} + x_{2}b_{2} + x_{3}b_{3} &= x \\\\\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + x_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + (-\\frac{1}{3})R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{x_{1} + 3x_{2} = 1; - 9x_{2} - x_{3} = 7; \\frac{4}{3}x_{3} = \\frac{8}{3}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2$. Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186118186 17592186118187 17592186118188 17592186118189 17592186118190] "immutable_fields" [[17592186118185 :answer-field/correct] [17592186118185 :answer-field/id] [17592186118185 :answer-field/key] [17592186118185 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
